# l3fwd

## description
This folder contains a directory with scripts to set up a systemd service for l3fwd testing.

The service, when enabled, does the following:
- disables ufw
- Creates routing rules, configurable with environment variables.
    ex: 
        For any packets from subnet 10.0.X.0/24 bound for subnet 10.0.Y.0/24 send them first to gateway address of 10.0.X.X

This (hopefully) makes it less painful to test l3fwd and testpmd on the same machine.
The 'ip' routing rules will not survive a reboot; but they will be re-applied as long as the l3fwd-ip-route.service is enabled. 
For a given environment, you set up the variables file and enable the service. When you want to switch back to testing testpmd, just disable the service and reboot.

## To create the variables file:
./create_variables_file.sh --gateway $gateway_ip --route-via $source_subnet --destination $destination_ip_address

## Then, to create and enable the service (first time setup):
./setup-ip-route.sh

## to disable the service and reset the default routing rules
sudo systemctl disable l3fwd-ip-route.service && sudo reboot

